1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,166
领导吃饭
lǐng dǎo chī fàn
The boss is eating.

2
00:00:01,166 --> 00:00:03,333
你转桌领导要夹菜了
nǐ zhuǎn zhuō lǐng dǎo yào jiā cài le
You turned the table when the boss was about to take food.

3
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:05,333
然后你把菜转走了
rán hòu nǐ bǎ cài zhuǎn zǒu le
Then you turned the food away.

4
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:07,166
领导开车门
lǐng dǎo kāi chē mén
The boss opens the car door.

5
00:00:07,166 --> 00:00:10,333
你上车领导开车门是要自己上车的
nǐ shàng chē lǐng dǎo kāi chē mén shì yào zì jǐ shàng chē de
You got in the car—when the boss opened the door, it was for themselves to get in.

6
00:00:10,333 --> 00:00:11,833
然后你上车了
rán hòu nǐ shàng chē le
Then you got in.

7
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:12,966
我就是那种人
wǒ jiù shì nà zhǒng rén
I’m that kind of person.

8
00:00:12,966 --> 00:00:14,100
就是听话听音
jiù shì tīng huà tīng yīn
The kind who listens between the lines.

9
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:15,900
我永远都听不懂领导在说什么
wǒ yǒng yuǎn dōu tīng bù dǒng lǐng dǎo zài shuō shén me
I can never understand what the boss is actually saying.

10
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:17,300
就是你听这个人说话
jiù shì nǐ tīng zhè ge rén shuō huà
When you listen to someone talk,

11
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,633
你不要听他说了什么字
nǐ bú yào tīng tā shuō le shén me zì
don’t just focus on the words they said.

12
00:00:19,633 --> 00:00:21,933
你要听他那个意思是什么
nǐ yào tīng tā nà ge yì si shì shén me
You need to understand what they mean.

13
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:25,233
中国人经常会说我改天请你吃饭
zhōng guó rén jīng cháng huì shuō wǒ gǎi tiān qǐng nǐ chī fàn
Chinese people often say “I'll treat you to a meal another day.”

14
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:27,100
其实他不是真的想请你吃饭
qí shí tā bú shì zhēn de xiǎng qǐng nǐ chī fàn
But they don’t actually mean it.

15
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:28,300
改天请你吃饭
gǎi tiān qǐng nǐ chī fàn
“I'll treat you another day”

16
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:32,433
意思就是我不会请你吃饭的意思
yì si jiù shì wǒ bú huì qǐng nǐ chī fàn de yì si
really means “I’m not going to treat you.”

17
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:36,566
大家好欢迎来到XiaoguaChinese的播客
dà jiā hǎo huān yíng lái dào Xiaogua Chinese de bō kè
Hi everyone, welcome to the Xiaogua Chinese podcast.

18
00:00:36,566 --> 00:00:38,333
今天呢我和Weixuan
jīn tiān ne wǒ hé Weixuan
Today Weixuan and I

19
00:00:38,333 --> 00:00:42,033
来跟大家分享一个特别有趣的
lái gēn dà jiā fēn xiǎng yí gè tè bié yǒu qù de
are going to share something really interesting with you.

20
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:45,200
和中国有关的东西
hé zhōng guó yǒu guān de dōng xī
Something related to China.

21
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,933
对那我们今天要讲的呢
duì nà wǒ men jīn tiān yào jiǎng de ne
Yes, and today what we want to talk about

22
00:00:47,933 --> 00:00:52,133
是跟中国人是怎么社交有关的
shì gēn zhōng guó rén shì zěn me shè jiāo yǒu guān de
is how Chinese people socialize.

23
00:00:52,133 --> 00:00:55,600
中国人有什么社交的礼仪
zhōng guó rén yǒu shén me shè jiāo de lǐ yí
What social etiquette do Chinese people have?

24
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:58,000
你需要注意什么
nǐ xū yào zhù yì shén me
What should you be aware of?

25
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,500
OK好
OK hǎo
OK, good.

26
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:00,900
Weixuan
Weixuan
Weixuan.

27
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:02,833
你准备好了吗
nǐ zhǔn bèi hǎo le ma
Are you ready?

28
00:01:02,833 --> 00:01:04,933
我准备好了来吧
wǒ zhǔn bèi hǎo le lái ba
I’m ready, let’s go.

29
00:01:04,933 --> 00:01:09,600
你是不是有很多故事要跟大家分享
nǐ shì bú shì yǒu hěn duō gù shì yào gēn dà jiā fēn xiǎng
Do you have a lot of stories to share with everyone?

30
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:13,733
对 我觉得虽然我没有工作很多很多年
duì wǒ jué de suī rán wǒ méi yǒu gōng zuò hěn duō hěn duō nián
Yes, although I haven’t worked for many many years,

31
00:01:13,733 --> 00:01:17,100
从我大学毕业到现在十年
cóng wǒ dà xué bì yè dào xiàn zài shí nián
It’s been ten years since I graduated from college.

32
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:21,166
然后我在公司工作 可能
rán hòu wǒ zài gōng sī gōng zuò kě néng
Then I worked in a company, maybe…

33
00:01:21,166 --> 00:01:22,900
我三年在非洲
wǒ sān nián zài fēi zhōu
I spent three years in Africa.

34
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:24,200
一年在北京
yì nián zài běi jīng
One year in Beijing.

35
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:26,366
然后三年在阿根廷
rán hòu sān nián zài ā gēn tíng
Then three years in Argentina.

36
00:01:26,366 --> 00:01:27,500
对7年
duì qī nián
Yes, seven years.

37
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:30,400
对还是有一些有一些工作经验的
duì hái shì yǒu yì xiē yǒu yì xiē gōng zuò jīng yàn de
Yes, so I do have some work experience.

38
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,233
可以跟大家分享一下
kě yǐ gēn dà jiā fēn xiǎng yí xià
I can share a bit with everyone.

39
00:01:33,233 --> 00:01:37,000
很好今天我来采访Weixuan
hěn hǎo jīn tiān wǒ lái cǎi fǎng Weixuan
Great. Today I’ll be interviewing Weixuan.

40
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,800
因为我没有太多经验
yīn wèi wǒ méi yǒu tài duō jīng yàn
Because I don’t have much experience.

41
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:42,900
基本上没有经验
jī běn shàng méi yǒu jīng yàn
Basically no experience.

42
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:44,533
那第一个就是
nà dì yī gè jiù shì
So the first one is…

43
00:01:44,533 --> 00:01:47,700
中国人说的关系
zhōng guó rén shuō de guān xì
The idea of “guanxi” that Chinese people talk about.

44
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:49,166
对那Weixuan
duì nà Weixuan
Right, so Weixuan…

45
00:01:49,166 --> 00:01:52,733
你对中国人说的关系
nǐ duì zhōng guó rén shuō de guān xì
What do you think about this idea of “guanxi”?

46
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:54,566
找关系
zhǎo guān xì
“Using connections”

47
00:01:54,566 --> 00:01:56,366
托关系
tuō guān xì
“Pulling strings”

48
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:58,800
这些你有什么理解
zhè xiē nǐ yǒu shén me lǐ jiě
What do you understand about these?

49
00:01:58,800 --> 00:01:59,400
关系
guān xì
Connections.

50
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,966
我觉得在中国文化里面是很重要的
wǒ jué de zài zhōng guó wén huà lǐ miàn shì hěn zhòng yào de
I think it’s very important in Chinese culture.

51
00:02:02,966 --> 00:02:06,366
比如说我在这个城市威海
bǐ rú shuō wǒ zài zhè ge chéng shì Wēi hǎi
For example, I was in the city of Weihai.

52
00:02:06,366 --> 00:02:07,900
然后呢
rán hòu ne
And then…

53
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:09,633
很小很小的事情
hěn xiǎo hěn xiǎo de shì qing
Even very small things—

54
00:02:09,633 --> 00:02:11,766
只要有一个事情
zhǐ yào yǒu yí gè shì qíng
As long as something happens,

55
00:02:11,766 --> 00:02:13,833
然后人们想的第一件事情是好
rán hòu rén men xiǎng de dì yī jiàn shì qíng shì hǎo
the first thing people think of is:

56
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:14,600
我去找一个
wǒ qù zhǎo yí gè
“I’ll find someone…”

57
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:15,633
我认识的人
wǒ rèn shi de rén
“someone I know.”

58
00:02:15,633 --> 00:02:18,600
我去看看我能不能有一些关系
wǒ qù kàn kàn wǒ néng bù néng yǒu yì xiē guān xì
Let me see if I can use some connections.

59
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:20,533
然后帮到我
rán hòu bāng dào wǒ
And let them help me.

60
00:02:20,533 --> 00:02:21,933
我给你举个例子啊
wǒ gěi nǐ jǔ gè lì zi a
Let me give you an example.

61
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:25,233
比如说很多孩子他们去上小学啊
bǐ rú shuō hěn duō hái zi tā men qù shàng xiǎo xué a
For example, many children are going to elementary school.

62
00:02:25,233 --> 00:02:26,900
那就去上小学嘛
nà jiù qù shàng xiǎo xué ma
So just go to school, right?

63
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:28,933
然后有老师对吧
rán hòu yǒu lǎo shī duì ba
And then there are teachers, right?

64
00:02:28,933 --> 00:02:32,366
但是总会有几个家长
dàn shì zǒng huì yǒu jǐ gè jiā zhǎng
But there will always be some parents

65
00:02:32,366 --> 00:02:34,833
就是小孩子的爸爸妈妈
jiù shì xiǎo hái zi de bà ba mā ma
The kid’s father or mother,

66
00:02:34,833 --> 00:02:36,166
他去找老师
tā qù zhǎo lǎo shī
They go talk to the teacher.

67
00:02:36,166 --> 00:02:37,233
他跟老师说
tā gēn lǎo shī shuō
They tell the teacher:

68
00:02:37,233 --> 00:02:40,033
我们孩子可能有一点调皮呀
wǒ men hái zi kě néng yǒu yì diǎn tiáo pí ya
“Our child might be a bit naughty…”

69
00:02:40,033 --> 00:02:42,966
啊他可能不是很会照顾自己呀
a tā kě néng bú shì hěn huì zhào gù zì jǐ ya
“He might not know how to take care of himself very well…”

70
00:02:42,966 --> 00:02:46,033
啊你一定要这个多照顾一下他
a nǐ yí dìng yào zhè ge duō zhào gù yí xià tā
“So please take extra care of him.”

71
00:02:46,033 --> 00:02:48,966
然后呢他会给老师送一些东西
rán hòu ne tā huì gěi lǎo shī sòng yì xiē dōng xi
And then they’ll give the teacher some gifts.

72
00:02:48,966 --> 00:02:50,333
但是不会送钱
dàn shì bú huì sòng qián
But they won’t give money.

73
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:52,233
他会给老师送一些礼物
tā huì gěi lǎo shī sòng yì xiē lǐ wù
They’ll give the teacher some presents.

74
00:02:52,233 --> 00:02:53,033
然后呢
rán hòu ne
And then…

75
00:02:53,033 --> 00:02:55,933
想让老师多照顾一下他的孩子
xiǎng ràng lǎo shī duō zhào gù yí xià tā de hái zi
They hope the teacher will give their child more attention.

76
00:02:55,933 --> 00:02:57,600
对这就是
duì zhè jiù shì
Yes, this is exactly

77
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:59,766
我们这个中国文化里面
wǒ men zhè ge zhōng guó wén huà lǐ miàn
what we often see in Chinese culture.

78
00:02:59,766 --> 00:03:02,166
经常有的一个关系
jīng cháng yǒu de yí gè guān xì
This kind of connection happens a lot.

79
00:03:02,166 --> 00:03:03,800
Weixuan说的这个关系
Weixuan shuō de zhè ge guān xì
The “guanxi” that Weixuan is talking about,

80
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,300
就是说
jiù shì shuō
it means

81
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:08,366
比如说你想解决一个问题
bǐ rú shuō nǐ xiǎng jiě jué yí gè wèn tí
if you want to solve a problem,

82
00:03:08,366 --> 00:03:09,933
你想做一件事情
nǐ xiǎng zuò yí jiàn shì qíng
you want to do something,

83
00:03:09,933 --> 00:03:11,233
你自己做不到
nǐ zì jǐ zuò bù dào
but you can’t do it by yourself,

84
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:13,133
但是你认识一些人
dàn shì nǐ rèn shi yì xiē rén
but you know some people,

85
00:03:13,133 --> 00:03:15,800
或者你跟他们建立一种关系
huò zhě nǐ gēn tā men jiàn lì yì zhǒng guān xì
or you’ve built some kind of relationship with them,

86
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,400
他们可以帮你
tā men kě yǐ bāng nǐ
then they can help you.

87
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:20,333
可以让你有一个很快的方法
kě yǐ ràng nǐ yǒu yí gè hěn kuài de fāng fǎ
They can give you a faster way

88
00:03:20,333 --> 00:03:22,366
好解决你不能解决的问题
hǎo jiě jué nǐ bù néng jiě jué de wèn tí
to solve something you couldn’t solve on your own.

89
00:03:22,366 --> 00:03:24,300
对嗯
duì en
Yes, exactly.

90
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:27,000
其实有的时候你找这个关系
qí shí yǒu de shí hòu nǐ zhǎo zhè ge guān xì
Actually, sometimes even if you try to use guanxi,

91
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,433
和你不找关系是一样的
hé nǐ bù zhǎo guān xì shì yí yàng de
it’s the same as not using it.

92
00:03:29,433 --> 00:03:31,500
比如看病吧
bǐ rú kàn bìng ba
For example, seeing a doctor.

93
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:31,933
然后
rán hòu
And then…

94
00:03:31,933 --> 00:03:35,733
这个医生可能要给这个病人做手术
zhè ge yī shēng kě néng yào gěi zhè ge bìng rén zuò shǒu shù
This doctor may need to perform surgery on a patient.

95
00:03:35,733 --> 00:03:37,033
你认识这个医生
nǐ rèn shi zhè ge yī shēng
You know the doctor,

96
00:03:37,033 --> 00:03:38,566
或者你不认识这个医生
huò zhě nǐ bù rèn shi zhè ge yī shēng
or you don’t know the doctor,

97
00:03:38,566 --> 00:03:41,366
他都会好好地给你做手术的
tā dōu huì hǎo hǎo de gěi nǐ zuò shǒu shù de
he will still do the surgery well.

98
00:03:41,366 --> 00:03:43,566
但是在中国的文化里面呢
dàn shì zài zhōng guó de wén huà lǐ miàn ne
But in Chinese culture,

99
00:03:43,566 --> 00:03:45,300
就会想啊
jiù huì xiǎng a
people will think:

100
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:48,533
我有一个朋友可能和这个医生认识
wǒ yǒu yí gè péng yǒu kě néng hé zhè ge yī shēng rèn shi
“I have a friend who might know the doctor.”

101
00:03:48,533 --> 00:03:50,233
那我要告诉这个朋友
nà wǒ yào gào sù zhè ge péng yǒu
“I’ll tell that friend.”

102
00:03:50,233 --> 00:03:51,133
然后呢
rán hòu ne
And then…

103
00:03:51,133 --> 00:03:54,200
我希望这个朋友告诉这个医生啊
wǒ xī wàng zhè ge péng yǒu gào sù zhè ge yī shēng a
I hope that friend will talk to the doctor,

104
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,800
好好地照顾我
hǎo hǎo de zhào gù wǒ
and ask them to take good care of me.

105
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,533
好好给我做手术
hǎo hǎo gěi wǒ zuò shǒu shù
To perform the surgery carefully.

106
00:03:57,533 --> 00:03:59,966
但是其实很多时候我觉得没有必要
dàn shì qí shí hěn duō shí hòu wǒ jué de méi yǒu bì yào
But honestly, a lot of times, I don’t think it’s necessary.

107
00:03:59,966 --> 00:04:00,800
对你
duì nǐ
Yeah, for you…

108
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:04,200
不管说不说你有没有这个关系
bù guǎn shuō bù shuō nǐ yǒu méi yǒu zhè ge guān xì
Whether or not you mention the connection,

109
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,333
结果是一样的
jié guǒ shì yí yàng de
the result is the same.

110
00:04:05,333 --> 00:04:06,733
我太同意了
wǒ tài tóng yì le
I totally agree.

111
00:04:06,733 --> 00:04:08,933
我特别受不了
wǒ tè bié shòu bù liǎo
I really can’t stand it.

112
00:04:08,933 --> 00:04:10,933
特别受不了我妈妈
tè bié shòu bù liǎo wǒ mā ma
I especially can’t stand my mom.

113
00:04:10,933 --> 00:04:14,300
因为对他一直只找一个医生
yīn wèi duì tā yī zhí zhǐ zhǎo yí gè yī shēng
Because she always only goes to one doctor.

114
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:17,500
因为那个是他的朋友的朋友
yīn wèi nà ge shì tā de péng yǒu de péng yǒu
Because that doctor is her friend’s friend.

115
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:20,700
那个他是一个妇科医生
nà ge tā shì yí gè fù kē yī shēng
That person is a gynecologist.

116
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:23,900
然后他帮我的嫂子
rán hòu tā bāng wǒ de sǎo zi
And he helped my sister-in-law

117
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:25,600
做了手术啊
zuò le shǒu shù a
do a surgery,

118
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:29,633
还有就是帮他顺利地生孩子
hái yǒu jiù shì bāng tā shùn lì de shēng hái zi
and also helped her give birth smoothly.

119
00:04:29,633 --> 00:04:31,133
然后我妈妈就会想
rán hòu wǒ mā ma jiù huì xiǎng
Then my mom would start thinking:

120
00:04:31,133 --> 00:04:33,833
我要不要给他包红包啊
wǒ yào bù yào gěi tā bāo hóng bāo a
Should I give him a red envelope?

121
00:04:33,833 --> 00:04:35,766
送他东西啊
sòng tā dōng xi a
Or send him gifts?

122
00:04:35,766 --> 00:04:38,366
我就觉得
wǒ jiù jué de
And I just feel like…

123
00:04:38,366 --> 00:04:40,200
啊
a
Ugh…

124
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:41,733
受不了受不了
shòu bù liǎo shòu bù liǎo
Can’t stand it, can’t stand it.

125
00:04:41,733 --> 00:04:44,433
这个就是非常非常中国的
zhè ge jiù shì fēi cháng fēi cháng zhōng guó de
This is just extremely Chinese.

126
00:04:44,433 --> 00:04:45,533
中国文化的
zhōng guó wén huà de
Part of Chinese culture.

127
00:04:45,533 --> 00:04:47,933
就是然后送红包
jiù shì rán hòu sòng hóng bāo
Giving red envelopes,

128
00:04:47,933 --> 00:04:49,100
然后送东西
rán hòu sòng dōng xi
Giving gifts,

129
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,633
是的然后你就觉得哦
shì de rán hòu nǐ jiù jué de ò
Yes, and then you feel like, oh…

130
00:04:50,633 --> 00:04:54,900
医生拿了红包才会认真地帮你做手术
yī shēng ná le hóng bāo cái huì rèn zhēn de bāng nǐ zuò shǒu shù
The doctor will only take your surgery seriously if they got a red envelope.

131
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:56,700
但是如果是一个好的医生
dàn shì rú guǒ shì yí gè hǎo de yī shēng
But if it’s a good doctor,

132
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:57,833
他就是会认真
tā jiù shì huì rèn zhēn
they’ll be responsible anyway.

133
00:04:57,833 --> 00:04:59,566
他就是会负责
tā jiù shì huì fù zé
They’ll take responsibility.

134
00:04:59,566 --> 00:05:01,700
对是的
duì shì de
Yes, exactly.

135
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:02,300
呃
e
Uh…

136
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:08,133
在中文里面有一句有一个词叫杀熟
zài zhōng wén lǐ miàn yǒu yí jù yǒu yí gè cí jiào shā shú
In Chinese, there’s a term called “shā shú.”

137
00:05:08,133 --> 00:05:10,166
它的意思就是
tā de yì si jiù shì
It means…

138
00:05:10,166 --> 00:05:11,933
越是熟悉的人
yuè shì shú xī de rén
The more familiar someone is,

139
00:05:11,933 --> 00:05:15,533
他可能他对你的下手越狠
tā kě néng tā duì nǐ de xià shǒu yuè hěn
the harsher they might treat you.

140
00:05:15,533 --> 00:05:18,233
反而你不认识这个人就还好
fǎn ér nǐ bú rèn shi zhè gè rén jiù hái hǎo
But if you don’t know them, they might treat you better.

141
00:05:18,233 --> 00:05:19,000
哈哈哈
hā hā hā
Haha.

142
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:23,566
比如说我之前在阿根廷工作的时候
bǐ rú shuō wǒ zhī qián zài ā gēn tíng gōng zuò de shí hòu
For example, when I was working in Argentina before…

143
00:05:23,566 --> 00:05:26,833
我们认识一个中国超市的老板
wǒ men rèn shi yí gè zhōng guó chāo shì de lǎo bǎn
We knew the owner of a Chinese supermarket.

144
00:05:26,833 --> 00:05:27,900
他人特别好
tā rén tè bié hǎo
He was really nice.

145
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:29,366
然后我们去买东西
rán hòu wǒ men qù mǎi dōng xī
Then we’d go buy things.

146
00:05:29,366 --> 00:05:30,000
他经常说
tā jīng cháng shuō
He would often say,

147
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,033
我给你打折啊
wǒ gěi nǐ dǎ zhé a
“I’ll give you a discount.”

148
00:05:31,033 --> 00:05:33,100
你多买一些东西啊
nǐ duō mǎi yì xiē dōng xī a
“Buy a bit more.”

149
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:35,600
然后呢我们就很相信他
rán hòu ne wǒ men jiù hěn xiàng xìn tā
So we trusted him a lot.

150
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:36,966
后来
hòu lái
Later on…

151
00:05:36,966 --> 00:05:39,033
我们经常吃火锅
wǒ men jīng cháng chī huǒ guō
We would often eat hotpot.

152
00:05:39,033 --> 00:05:40,300
然后到周末的时候
rán hòu dào zhōu mò de shí hòu
And on weekends,

153
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:41,433
我们就给他打电话
wǒ men jiù gěi tā dǎ diàn huà
we’d give him a call.

154
00:05:41,433 --> 00:05:42,100
我们说哎
wǒ men shuō āi
We’d say, “Hey…”

155
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:43,433
老板这个
lǎo bǎn zhè ge
“Boss, this…”

156
00:05:43,433 --> 00:05:45,966
这个星期今天晚上我们要吃火锅
zhè gè xīng qī jīn tiān wǎn shàng wǒ men yào chī huǒ guō
“We’re having hotpot tonight.”

157
00:05:45,966 --> 00:05:47,333
你给我们准备些肉
nǐ gěi wǒ men zhǔn bèi xiē ròu
“Can you prepare some meat for us…”

158
00:05:47,333 --> 00:05:49,133
还有菜然后你就放在那里
hái yǒu cài rán hòu nǐ jiù fàng zài nà lǐ
“and vegetables, then leave them there.”

159
00:05:49,133 --> 00:05:51,200
我们下班就去拿
wǒ men xià bān jiù qù ná
“We’ll pick them up after work.”

160
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:54,233
然后呢我们不会问他这个肉多少钱
rán hòu ne wǒ men bú huì wèn tā zhè gè ròu duō shǎo qián
And we never asked him how much the meat cost.

161
00:05:54,233 --> 00:05:55,766
这个菜多少钱
zhè gè cài duō shǎo qián
Or the vegetables.

162
00:05:55,766 --> 00:05:57,100
这个饮料多少钱
zhè gè yǐn liào duō shǎo qián
Or the drinks.

163
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:59,333
我们去了就直接给他钱
wǒ men qù le jiù zhí jiē gěi tā qián
We’d just go and pay him directly.

164
00:05:59,333 --> 00:06:01,933
然后我们就走了
rán hòu wǒ men jiù zǒu le
And then we’d leave.

165
00:06:01,933 --> 00:06:04,166
但是其实是很意外的
dàn shì qí shí shì hěn yì wài de
But actually, it was quite unexpected.

166
00:06:04,166 --> 00:06:06,033
有一次他说
yǒu yí cì tā shuō
One time he said,

167
00:06:06,033 --> 00:06:07,566
那次他生病了
nà cì tā shēng bìng le
That time he was sick.

168
00:06:07,566 --> 00:06:08,800
然后呢他说啊
rán hòu ne tā shuō a
Then he said,

169
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:10,366
我今天我不舒服
wǒ jīn tiān wǒ bù shū fú
“I’m not feeling well today.”

170
00:06:10,366 --> 00:06:12,766
你们去别家买吧
nǐ men qù bié jiā mǎi ba
“You guys go buy from another store.”

171
00:06:12,766 --> 00:06:15,300
然后我们就去别人家买了东西
rán hòu wǒ men jiù qù bié rén jiā mǎi le dōng xī
So we went to someone else’s store and bought the stuff.

172
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:19,400
我们发现价格差了很多
wǒ men fā xiàn jià gé chà le hěn duō
We realized the price difference was huge.

173
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:21,233
差很多
chà hěn duō
It was way off.

174
00:06:21,233 --> 00:06:24,366
对然后我就觉得哎
duì rán hòu wǒ jiù jué de āi
Yeah, and then I thought,

175
00:06:24,366 --> 00:06:26,233
他为什么要这样做
tā wèi shén me yào zhè yàng zuò
Why would he do that?

176
00:06:26,233 --> 00:06:28,200
后来我们想了一下
hòu lái wǒ men xiǎng le yí xià
Later we thought about it.

177
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:31,633
可能就是因为我们很熟认识
kě néng jiù shì yīn wèi wǒ men hěn shú rèn shi
Maybe it’s because we were close and knew each other well.

178
00:06:31,633 --> 00:06:32,633
然后他觉得
rán hòu tā jué de
And he thought,

179
00:06:32,633 --> 00:06:35,333
你们不会怀疑我的价钱有问题
nǐ men bú huì huái yí wǒ de jià qián yǒu wèn tí
“You guys wouldn’t question my pricing.”

180
00:06:35,333 --> 00:06:37,700
嗯啊那我就告诉你个价钱
ń a nà wǒ jiù gào sù nǐ gè jià qián
“So I’ll just give you a price.”

181
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:39,833
然后你们就给我钱就好了
rán hòu nǐ men jiù gěi wǒ qián jiù hǎo le
“And you’ll just pay me.”

182
00:06:39,833 --> 00:06:41,300
嗯嗯对
ń ń duì
Yeah, right.

183
00:06:41,300 --> 00:06:45,033
所以我觉得关系有的时候很熟
suǒ yǐ wǒ jué de guān xì yǒu de shí hòu hěn shú
So I think sometimes being close in a relationship…

184
00:06:45,033 --> 00:06:47,000
不一定是一个好的事情
bù yí dìng shì yí gè hǎo de shì qíng
isn’t necessarily a good thing.

185
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:47,900
对对对对对
duì duì duì duì duì
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

186
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:51,900
有可能会是一个杀熟
yǒu kě néng huì shì yí gè shā shú
It could end up being a “shā shú” situation.

187
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:53,133
对对对
duì duì duì
Exactly.

188
00:06:53,133 --> 00:06:55,166
好那第二点呢
hǎo nà dì èr diǎn ne
Okay, now the second point,

189
00:06:55,166 --> 00:06:59,566
也是跟这个中国人怎么社交有关系的
yě shì gēn zhè ge zhōng guó rén zěn me shè jiāo yǒu guān xì de
is also related to how Chinese people socialize.

190
00:06:59,566 --> 00:07:03,300
就是我们会含蓄地拒绝
jiù shì wǒ men huì hán xù de jù jué
We tend to reject things indirectly.

191
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:07,000
不会直接说不不可以
bú huì zhí jiē shuō bù bù kě yǐ
We don’t directly say “no” or “you can’t.”

192
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,566
我不行我不能
wǒ bù xíng wǒ bù néng
“I can’t, I’m not able to.”

193
00:07:09,566 --> 00:07:13,933
对Weixuan你也是这样子拒绝别人的吗
duì Weixuan nǐ yě shì zhè yàng zi jù jué bié rén de ma
Weixuan, do you also reject people like this?

194
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:19,166
对对对对我有的时候会说哦行
duì duì duì duì wǒ yǒu de shí hòu huì shuō ò xíng
Yes, yes, sometimes I’ll say, “Okay, sure.”

195
00:07:19,166 --> 00:07:20,233
那再说吧
nà zài shuō ba
“Let’s talk about it later.”

196
00:07:20,233 --> 00:07:22,333
哈哈以后再说吧
hā hā yǐ hòu zài shuō ba
Haha, “We’ll talk about it another time.”

197
00:07:22,333 --> 00:07:25,533
嗯我不会说不行
ń wǒ bú huì shuō bù xíng
Yeah, I won’t say “no.”

198
00:07:25,533 --> 00:07:27,966
对不可以我不去
duì bù kě yǐ wǒ bù qù
Right, or “I can’t” or “I won’t go.”

199
00:07:27,966 --> 00:07:29,966
是的对那样不太好
shì de duì nà yàng bú tài hǎo
Exactly. That doesn’t feel polite.

200
00:07:29,966 --> 00:07:33,766
对对对所以大家要怎么说呢
duì duì duì suǒ yǐ dà jiā yào zěn me shuō ne
Yes, so how do people say it?

201
00:07:33,766 --> 00:07:40,433
要日语里面叫做读空气
yào rì yǔ lǐ miàn jiào zuò dú kōng qì
In Japanese it’s called “reading the air.”

202
00:07:40,433 --> 00:07:44,100
对英语里面有一个read between the lines
duì yīng yǔ lǐ miàn yǒu yí gè “read between the lines”
Yeah, in English it’s “read between the lines.”

203
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:50,700
我不知道中文是什么就是
wǒ bù zhī dào zhōng wén shì shén me jiù shì
I don’t know how to say it in Chinese, just…

204
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:54,766
你要听懂他没有说的东西
nǐ yào tīng dǒng tā méi yǒu shuō de dōng xī
You have to understand what they didn’t say.

205
00:07:54,766 --> 00:07:57,600
就是如果这个人说再说吧
jiù shì rú guǒ zhè ge rén shuō zài shuō ba
Like, if someone says “let’s talk later,”

206
00:07:57,600 --> 00:08:00,700
他也没有跟你定什么时候再说
tā yě méi yǒu gēn nǐ dìng shén me shí hòu zài shuō
but they didn’t set a time for that,

207
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:04,133
那有可能他不想跟你说这个
nà yǒu kě néng tā bù xiǎng gēn nǐ shuō zhè ge
then maybe they don’t really want to talk about it.

208
00:08:04,133 --> 00:08:05,533
他想要说不
tā xiǎng yào shuō bù
They actually want to say “no.”

209
00:08:05,533 --> 00:08:09,000
他没有非常感兴趣
tā méi yǒu fēi cháng gǎn xìng qù
They’re not really interested.

210
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,300
对他觉得再说吧
duì tā jué de zài shuō ba
Yeah, they think “let’s talk later” means…

211
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:15,233
意思是我以后可能就把这件事情忘记了
yì si shì wǒ yǐ hòu kě néng jiù bǎ zhè jiàn shì qíng wàng jì le
“It’s likely I’ll just forget about it later.”

212
00:08:15,233 --> 00:08:18,000
意思就是我我不感兴趣我不想
yì si jiù shì wǒ wǒ bù gǎn xìng qù wǒ bù xiǎng
Meaning I’m not interested, I don’t want to.

213
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:22,133
中文里面我觉得是听话听音
zhōng wén lǐ miàn wǒ jué de shì tīng huà tīng yīn
In Chinese, I think it’s “listen between the lines.”

214
00:08:22,133 --> 00:08:23,566
就是你听这个人说话
jiù shì nǐ tīng zhè ge rén shuō huà
It means when you listen to someone speak,

215
00:08:23,566 --> 00:08:25,800
你不要听他说了什么字
nǐ bú yào tīng tā shuō le shén me zì
don’t just focus on the actual words.

216
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:29,233
你要听他那个意思是什么
nǐ yào tīng tā nà gè yì si shì shén me
You need to understand the meaning behind them.

217
00:08:29,233 --> 00:08:30,900
对听话听音
duì tīng huà tīng yīn
Yes, “listening between the lines.”

218
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:33,733
啊这个我没听过
a zhè ge wǒ méi tīng guò
Ah, I haven’t heard that before.

219
00:08:33,733 --> 00:08:35,233
我也没用过
wǒ yě méi yòng guò
I’ve never used it either.

220
00:08:35,233 --> 00:08:37,600
但是我可以可以理解
dàn shì wǒ kě yǐ kě yǐ lǐ jiě
But I can understand it.

221
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:40,800
对那你有没有试过
duì nà nǐ yǒu méi yǒu shì guò
Yeah, have you ever experienced…

222
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:44,100
就是啊我觉得这个很搞笑
jiù shì a wǒ jué de zhè gè hěn gǎo xiào
I think this is really funny,

223
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:45,733
因为不同的文化
yīn wèi bù tóng de wén huà
because in different cultures,

224
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:48,766
拒绝拒绝是不一样的嘛
jù jué jù jué shì bù yí yàng de ma
refusal is expressed differently, right?

225
00:08:48,766 --> 00:08:51,233
所以比如说对呃
suǒ yǐ bǐ rú shuō duì e
So for example…

226
00:08:51,233 --> 00:08:53,966
有一个有一个中国朋友
yǒu yí gè yǒu yí gè zhōng guó péng yǒu
There was a Chinese friend.

227
00:08:53,966 --> 00:08:55,533
他拒绝了
tā jù jué le
They refused.

228
00:08:55,533 --> 00:08:57,600
他说以后再说
tā shuō yǐ hòu zài shuō
They said, “let’s talk later.”

229
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:01,533
但是那个人他就真的以后再说
dàn shì nà gè rén tā jiù zhēn de yǐ hòu zài shuō
But the other person really followed up later.

230
00:09:01,533 --> 00:09:03,133
就来找他说
jiù lái zhǎo tā shuō
And came back to ask him,

231
00:09:03,133 --> 00:09:06,833
上次我们说的那件事情怎么样了
shàng cì wǒ men shuō de nà jiàn shì qíng zěn me yàng le
“How’s that thing we talked about last time?”

232
00:09:06,833 --> 00:09:10,033
对对或者是有一些不同文化的人
duì duì huò zhě shì yǒu yì xiē bù tóng wén huà de rén
Yes, or people from different cultures…

233
00:09:10,033 --> 00:09:12,733
我记得有西班牙的朋友也是
wǒ jì de yǒu xī bān yá de péng yǒu yě shì
I remember I had a Spanish friend too.

234
00:09:12,733 --> 00:09:15,533
他说他打电话给中国客户
tā shuō tā dǎ diàn huà gěi zhōng guó kè hù
He said he called his Chinese clients.

235
00:09:15,533 --> 00:09:19,400
他们经常说我再考虑考虑
tā men jīng cháng shuō wǒ zài kǎo lǜ kǎo lǜ
They often said, “I’ll think about it.”

236
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:20,733
我再想想
wǒ zài xiǎng xiǎng
“I’ll think it over.”

237
00:09:20,733 --> 00:09:22,366
人家意思是说不
rén jiā yì si shì shuō bù
What they actually meant was “no.”

238
00:09:22,366 --> 00:09:24,166
但是他理解的是哎
dàn shì tā lǐ jiě de shì āi
But he understood it as, “Oh…”

239
00:09:24,166 --> 00:09:25,833
你考虑好了吗
nǐ kǎo lǜ hǎo le ma
“Have you thought it over?”

240
00:09:25,833 --> 00:09:29,166
你要买吗哈哈哈
nǐ yào mǎi ma hā hā hā
“Are you going to buy it?” Hahaha.

241
00:09:29,166 --> 00:09:30,900
然后他就问人家嗯
rán hòu tā jiù wèn rén jiā ń
Then he asked them again,

242
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:32,366
你考虑好了吗对对对
nǐ kǎo lǜ hǎo le ma duì duì duì
“Have you made a decision?” Right, right, right.

243
00:09:32,366 --> 00:09:34,233
对对对嗯
duì duì duì ń
Yes, exactly.

244
00:09:34,233 --> 00:09:37,133
你有过这样子的误会吗
nǐ yǒu guò zhè yàng zi de wù huì ma
Have you ever had this kind of misunderstanding?

245
00:09:37,133 --> 00:09:38,000
我有过
wǒ yǒu guò
Yes, I have.

246
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:44,033
就是中国人经常会说我改天请你吃饭
jiù shì zhōng guó rén jīng cháng huì shuō wǒ gǎi tiān qǐng nǐ chī fàn
Chinese people often say, “I’ll treat you to a meal another day.”

247
